# Data artifacts always go through Git LFS so the repository history stays
# small: the index keeps a ~130-byte pointer instead of the file itself.
#
# The rules are by extension on purpose. Matching only `datos/` is what allowed
# a 16 MB duplicate of the dataset to be committed under `ml/datos/` in #44 and
# be copied into every clone from then on.
#
# See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md (Git LFS requirement) and
# scripts/validate-artifacts.mjs (the check that fails when a data artifact
# reaches the index without LFS).
*.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
